From 95c741b84224c27422950197022a8ad64f9d1435 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObliviOS Build <build@oblivios.local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:43:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] compartments: give an app with a persona a standing fix while
 the phone has no real fix

An app whose location is substituted and that has a place is given the fixes of
a receiver that stands at the place when no real fix reaches it (ADR-214, CMP-047):
a wakeup alarm per active registration of the gps, fused and network providers
delivers a fix 3 s after the registration began or the last real fix arrived, then
once per request interval, through the same filters, permission level and app-op
note as a real fix. getLastLocation answers with the newer of the real last
location and the standing fix. The fix is kept per app in PersonaTrack (new
StandingFix: a mean-reverting walk, a bounded accuracy, times 20 to 60 ms before
the delivery, a stationary speed, no altitude, bearing, extras or mock flag), so
gps and fused agree, and the first real fix after it continues from the last
standing position. A real fix at 1.5 m/s or more holds the standing fix back for
120 s; an emergency gets no standing fix. The shared last-location table is
untouched; the distance filter of a request ignores the distance between a real and
a standing fix.
---
